Subject: SDK streaming snippet + routing example

Alex / Priya — quick code samples below. These are minimal; we'll provide language-specific libs if you want.

// WebSocket streaming (JS)
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://api.redwood.ai/v1/stream?model=redwood-chat-xl');
ws.onopen = () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({api_key: 'REDACTED', request: {type: 'chat', messages: [{role: 'user', content: 'Ticket: user cannot login...'}], stream: true}}));
};
ws.onmessage = (evt) => {
  const chunk = JSON.parse(evt.data);
  // chunk.type can be 'token', 'event', 'tool_call', 'end'
  if (chunk.type === 'token') appendToUI(chunk.text);
};

// Routing header example (HTTP)
POST /v1/chat HTTP/1.1
Host: api.redwood.ai
Authorization: Bearer <SERVICE_KEY_FOR_ZEPHYR_PROD>
X-Redwood-Routing: cluster=dedicated-us-west;fallback=hosted

Notes: the routing header is optional; keys can also be pre-bound in the console to a specific cluster.

Also: for reranker batch jobs, use the /v1/score endpoint with content-type application/json and include truncation strategies so you don't blow past token quotas.

Let me know which SDK language you prefer (TS/Go/Python).

—Dev
Senior Solutions Engineer, Redwood Inference
